@echo off
setlocal EnableExtensions
title Capri on live XyberRP: her brain, her own voice, Mass Override for everyone
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem   Two things only one PC had, for every player on LIVE XyberRP (Staging had them first, C2,
rem   and you checked them in game):
rem   HER OWN VOICE.  A PC speaks with her real voice only when it installed her local engine
rem   (about 900 MB); every other PC borrowed a Windows voice.  Her same engine and voice files
rem   now run on the game servers' machine, and every player's Capri Voz uses them on launch.  A
rem   PC with her local engine keeps using it; a player's own voice choice stays.
rem   MASS OVERRIDE FOR EVERYONE.  A cast showed on the caster's screen only: the other games never
rem   heard of it.  Now every game follows the gate from its start, and runs every cast near it --
rem   the street around the caster, and the city's lights and billboards for everyone.
rem   NOBODY MAY BE ON XyberRP: the package change refuses while anybody is on it.
rem   1. Her voice on the machine, once for the whole machine (C2 put it there: this only checks it):
rem      Pocket TTS with her voice files from XyberRP's own package, a test line in English and Spanish, its
rem      own service, and its own private address in the web server with a limit per address --
rem      the web server is checked and put back by itself on any failure.  Then one line in each
rem      language from this PC, the way a player's Capri Voz asks it.  The first time takes a few
rem      minutes (about 1.5 GB is downloaded on the machine).
rem   2. XyberRP's Mass Override gate updated (it keeps working for older builds), asked from here.
rem   3. The new Capri package: the live one with the brain wired in, Mass Override for every
rem      player, and Capri Voz speaking with her voice from the server -- checked with YOUR GAME'S
rem      OWN Redscript compiler and PowerShell's own parser on this PC; nothing is sent unless both
rem      pass.  Then it goes into XyberRP's mod store and server.jsonc names it (kept first).
rem   4. The brain's per-address limits (once for the machine; nothing when they are there).
rem   5. XyberRP restarted: players get the new Capri from the launcher when they join.
rem   6. READ ONLY: what XyberRP hands out now, checked end to end, her voice asked again.
rem   Nothing else changes: Staging, the brain and the other mods stay as they are.
rem   Logs: kit\capri-*.log here, and ..\open77-av-kit\avkit-restart-*.log.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
set "PY=%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\fivem2open77\runtime\python\python.exe"
if not exist "%PY%" goto nopython
set "CK=%~dp0kit\capri_kit.py"
if not exist "%CK%" goto nokit
set "AVK="
if exist "%~dp0..\open77-av-kit\av_kit.py" set "AVK=%~dp0..\open77-av-kit"
if not defined AVK if exist "%USERPROFILE%\Downloads\open77-av-kit\av_kit.py" set "AVK=%USERPROFILE%\Downloads\open77-av-kit"
if not defined AVK goto noavkit
set "AV=%AVK%\av_kit.py"
set "O77_AV_KIT=%AVK%"
@@HOST@@

echo.
echo Next: her own voice and Mass Override for everyone on LIVE XyberRP.  Nobody may be on
echo XyberRP (you neither): the package change refuses while anybody is on it.
choice /C YN /M "Do it on live XyberRP now"
if errorlevel 2 goto declined
echo.
set "RG=0"
echo === 1. Her own voice on the game servers' machine (the first time takes a few minutes)
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" voice --role production %HOST%
set "RVO=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RVO%"=="0" goto novoice
echo.
echo === 2. XyberRP's Mass Override gate: every game gets every cast
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" gate --role production %HOST%
set "RGA=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RGA%"=="0" goto nogate
echo.
echo === 3. The new Capri for XyberRP: built, checked with your game's Redscript, put on XyberRP
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" publish --role production %HOST%
set "RC=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if "%RC%"=="5" goto already
if not "%RC%"=="0" goto notpublished
call :guard
echo.
echo === 5. XyberRP restarted: players get the new Capri when they join
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%AV%" restart --on open77-xbuniverse --production %HOST%
set "RS=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RS%"=="0" goto notrestarted
:verify
echo.
echo === 6. READ ONLY: what XyberRP hands out now
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" verify --role production %HOST%
set "RV=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if not "%RV%"=="0" goto notverified
if not "%RG%"=="0" echo (Step 4 did NOT add the brain's per-address limits: see its lines above.)
echo.
echo Done.  Now on BOTH PCs (the laptop and the desktop):
echo   1. join XyberRP through the Open77 launcher: it names Capri's new build and asks
echo      once before installing it (it carries a DLL) -- accept;
echo   2. load in: on the desktop her greeting should NOT mention a Windows voice, and she speaks
echo      with her own voice (it comes from the server: the first line can take a second or two);
echo   3. stand near each other and have Capri cast Mass Override on one PC ("Capri, mass
echo      override"): the other PC's street, lights and billboards should go too, within a couple
echo      of seconds;
echo   4. then run C1 here: it shows her voice's last lines and every game the gate saw run a cast.
echo Then tell Claude how it went.
pause
exit /b 0

:already
echo.
echo XyberRP's Capri package already has all of this: nothing changed in it.
call :guard
goto verify

:guard
echo.
echo === 4. The brain's per-address limits (its private address goes to every player)
"%PY%" -X utf8 "%CK%" guard %HOST%
set "RG=%ERRORLEVEL%"
exit /b 0

:declined
echo.
echo Nothing done, nothing changed.
pause
exit /b 0

:novoice
echo.
echo Her voice is NOT on the machine (exit %RVO%): see the lines above, and tell Claude "done".
echo Nothing else was changed: the gate and XyberRP's Capri package are as they were.
pause
exit /b %RVO%

:nogate
echo.
echo XyberRP's Mass Override gate was NOT updated, or it does not answer (exit %RGA%): the old
echo gate is back if anything failed.  XyberRP's Capri package was not changed.  Tell Claude "done".
pause
exit /b %RGA%

:notpublished
echo.
echo XyberRP's Capri was NOT changed (exit %RC%): see the lines above, and tell Claude "done".
echo (exit 3: somebody is on XyberRP -- you too count -- or its Capri changed meanwhile: leave
echo it and run this again.  exit 2: this PC could not check the package with your game's
echo Redscript -- the lines above say why.  exit 1: something else; nothing was sent.)
echo Her voice and the gate (steps 1-2) are in place and harmless without the new package.
pause
exit /b %RC%

:notrestarted
echo.
echo XyberRP's server.jsonc names the new Capri, but XyberRP did not restart (exit %RS%).  exit 3:
echo somebody joined meanwhile -- leave it and run this again (the change is in, the restart is
echo what is missing).  exit 4: the Open77 master server refused the start for now: XyberRP is
echo stopped, run this again in a few minutes.  Tell Claude "done".
pause
exit /b %RS%

:notverified
echo.
echo XyberRP restarted, but what it hands out is not checked yet (exit %RV%): see the lines above
echo and tell Claude "done".  C3b puts XyberRP's Capri back.
pause
exit /b %RV%

:nopython
echo FAILED: fivem2open77 Studio's Python is not at %PY% - is the Studio installed?
pause
exit /b 1

:nokit
echo FAILED: this folder's own kit (kit\capri_kit.py) is missing: unpack the whole folder again.
pause
exit /b 1

:noavkit
echo FAILED: the AV kit's av_kit.py was not found: not in %~dp0..\open77-av-kit, not in
echo %USERPROFILE%\Downloads\open77-av-kit.  It signs in to the machine the way the Studio does.
pause
exit /b 1
